<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  HealthKit, and only HealthKit.

	  **This was believed impossible on this project for a long time, and that was wrong.**
	  `docs/decisions.md` recorded "No HealthKit (signing fails on a personal team)" as a hard
	  constraint, and every surface that mentioned it repeated the claim. It was never tested: the
	  repository contains no `import HealthKit` before this change.

	  Verified by probing rather than by argument — a throwaway target signed with the same free
	  Personal Team and produced a profile carrying `com.apple.developer.healthkit`,
	  `…healthkit.background-delivery` and `…healthkit.access`. So this key alone is enough, and a
	  paid account is not required for it.

	  No `com.apple.developer.healthkit.background-delivery` here: that is for `HKObserverQuery`
	  background delivery, which Oronzo does not use — it writes one workout when a session ends
	  and never reads anything back.

	  The Watch target deliberately has no entitlement and no entry here. It renders the session;
	  the phone owns it, and the phone is what writes to Health.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
